; Alpaca — model scene for AnimalDefinition.model_scenes.
; Source: Quaternius "Ultimate Animated Animal Pack" (July 2021), CC0 1.0 — same pack as
; Fox; see project/attribution/sources/quaternius_ultimate_animated_animals.tres.
;
; Design role: art.md → Newly Available Animals proposes open_grass · Bold · "exotic-cute
; grazer." Not locked design.
;
; Audit (2026-07-26): 13 animation clips confirmed — Idle, Idle_2, Idle_Headlow,
; Idle_HitReact1/2, Walk, Gallop, Gallop_Jump, Jump_toIdle, Eating, Attack_Headbutt,
; Attack_Kick, Death. Idle/Walk both present and non-degenerate (48 tracks each). Node
; structure matches Fox (AnimalArmature -> Skeleton3D -> mesh; AnimationPlayer sibling
; index 1).
;
; STYLE/SCALE NOTE (flag, not a rejection per this task's non-floor rule): raw AABB height
; is 5.398 units — taller than Horse (4.824) and almost as tall as Stag (5.378), which
; does not match a real alpaca's proportions (shorter than a horse). This is measured off
; the model's rest/bind pose, not its Idle clip frame, and alpacas are commonly rigged
; with an alert, neck-up rest pose that reads much taller than the animal's relaxed
; standing height — likely the cause, but this wrapper does not correct it, since no
; mesh-level fix is available in this pipeline and the correct call is the human's eyeball
; judgment against the rest of the roster at the same table (per art.md's Visual Style
; "readability" rule and this task's Boundary note).
;
; Scale: 0.2, matching Fox's established factor for this pack (same rationale as
; Deer.tscn) — kept uniform rather than compensating for the pose issue above with a
; one-off number. Scaled height would be 1.080 at this factor. FLAGGED FOR HUMAN REVIEW.
